o highlight the scientific aspect over the compliance aspect. The value is in the *empirical study of drift and failure modes in production*.\n\n    *   ID: P2245\n    *   Rationale: Developing quantitative thresholds for performance drift and adverse-event detection in live biometric systems provides essential empirical data on model reliability and stability in real-world settings. This operationalizes AI observability, turning compliance logs into a dataset for studying the lifecycle of high-risk AI.\n    *   Decision: approve\n    *   Promise: 75 (High value for safety/reliability research, though framed as compliance).",
