nical documentation required for compliance. While Article 12 focuses heavily on operational logs (\"events\" during use), Recital 71 explicitly links this to how systems were developed. Automating the \"hand-off\" from research to deployment ensures that the records needed for high-risk classification are already present.\n\n    *   *Rationale:* This proposal optimizes current MLOps infrastructure to automate regulatory documentation, eliminating redundant administrative overhead and enhancing scientific reproducibility. It directly supports Article 12/Recital 71 requirements by embedding provenance into the R&D workflow rather than treating compliance as a post-hoc manual task.\n    *   *Decision:* Approve.\n    *   *Promise:* Very high. Automating documentation is always a win for resource efficiency and reduces human error in regulatory filings.\n\n    *   Rationale: 1-2 sentences. (Check)\n    *   Decision: \"approve\" or \"reject\". (Check)\n    *   Promise: Integer 0-100. (Check)\n    *   ID echoed exactly: P2895. (Check)",
