osal treats a regulatory requirement as a design constraint. This is standard professional practice in industrial R&D.\n    *   By automating the logging via an SDK, it minimizes the \"tax\" on researchers while ensuring that the scientific output (the AI system) remains viable for actual use-cases (market access).\n    *   From a research integrity standpoint, having robust logs of inputs and reference databases actually *improves* intellectual merit by providing better traceability and reproducibility.\n\n    *   Rationale: Automating record-keeping via a standardized SDK ensures the reproducibility and auditability of high-risk systems without placing an undue implementation burden on individual researchers. This allows us to maintain scientific rigor while ensuring our research can be legally transitioned from development to real-world impact.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: High (85-90), because it's a practical infrastructure play that supports the ultimate goal of impactful, deployable AI research.",
