mentally aligned with good scientific practice (reproducibility, auditability). If the researchers are the ones burdened by this \"steward,\" it might be annoying; if the steward *helps* capture the research process so the researcher doesn't have to do it manually at the end, it's a win.\n\n    *   The proposal is focused on governance and compliance (the \"how\" of documentation).\n    *   While not an AI research breakthrough itself, maintaining precise records of algorithms, data, and testing processes is critical for scientific integrity and reproducibility.\n    *   Ensuring that the knowledge created during R&D isn't lost or becomes \"stale\" supports the long-term intellectual merit of the work by creating a reliable archive of development iterations.\n\n    *   Rationale: While primarily administrative, maintaining rigorous, up-to-date documentation of training data and algorithms is essential for scientific reproducibility and ensures that the intellectual provenance of our research is preserved.\n    *   Decision: Approve (It's necessary for the integrity of the R&D process, even if it isn't \"research\" itself).\n    *   Promise: 75 (High value for stability and rigor, though low on \"innovation\").",
