ild\" but not \"the maintenance.\" This proposal solves a structural problem that would otherwise jeopardize compliance and scientific rigor.\n\n    *   The proposal isn't about *how* to log, but *how to pay* for logging/documentation.\n    *   From a researcher's perspective: Unfunded mandates are the death of good science. If I have to spend my research budget on AWS S3 buckets for logs just to satisfy Article 12, I can't buy GPUs or hire post-docs. This proposal protects the intellectual merit of projects by decoupling compliance costs from research budgets.\n\n    *   Rationale: Ensuring long-term funding for documentation and logging prevents the degradation of scientific traceability over a system's lifetime and protects core research budgets from being cannibalized by regulatory overhead.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (85-90). It addresses a critical practical barrier to sustainable high-risk AI research.",
