sal doesn't explicitly mention anonymization, but it's for *internal* audit data used in reports already produced. As Compliance Officer, I would insist on data minimization/privacy controls, but the concept of using logs for risk assessment is fundamentally sound and encouraged by the spirit of the Act (monitoring performance throughout lifetime).\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal leverages a regulatory mandate to strengthen our internal risk-management and post-market monitoring capabilities without requiring additional funding. It directly aligns with the EU AI Act's goals of traceability and operational monitoring while improving the scientific robustness of our systems.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (e.g., 90), because it turns a cost center (compliance logging) into a value-add for both science and regulatory safety.",
